From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:30:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: smb358: start source changes at 500 mA

Keep source attachment and temperature recovery at the conservative 500 mA
baseline. The previous DCP path jumped directly to the DT ceiling before
the userspace one-second input-current ramp could observe the new source.
Let that policy increase the standard input_current_limit only after valid
feedback. Keep hardware AICL, battery charge current, float voltage,
termination and temperature inhibition unchanged.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/smb347-charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/smb347-charger.c
--- a/drivers/power/supply/smb347-charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/smb347-charger.c
@@ -214,7 +214,6 @@
 	struct notifier_block extcon_nb;
 	struct work_struct source_work;
 	struct mutex input_lock;
-	unsigned int dcp_current_limit;
 
 	struct device		*dev;
 	struct regmap		*regmap;
@@ -790,14 +789,10 @@
 {
 	struct smb347_charger *smb = container_of(work, struct smb347_charger,
 						 source_work);
-	unsigned int ua = 500000;
 	int ret;
 
-	if (extcon_get_state(smb->extcon, EXTCON_CHG_USB_DCP) > 0 &&
-	    (!smb->temperature_channel || smb->temperature_allowed))
-		ua = smb->dcp_current_limit;
-
-	ret = smb358_set_input_limit(smb, ua);
+	/* Userspace may ramp up after observing the source; never jump on attach. */
+	ret = smb358_set_input_limit(smb, 500000);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(smb->dev, "failed to set source current limit: %d\n", ret);
 		return;
@@ -1812,7 +1807,6 @@
 		if (IS_ERR(smb->extcon))
 			return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(smb->extcon),
 					     "failed to get source detector\n");
-		smb->dcp_current_limit = smb->usb_hc_current_limit;
 		smb->usb_hc_current_limit = 500000;
 	}
 	if (!smb->use_mains && !smb->use_usb)
